 "standard_text": "Solve simple linear equations by balancing; form equations from word problems and solve them. (summary of the NERDC JSS 1 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free JSS 1 maths worksheets on simple linear equations: one-step and two-step equations, equations with brackets, and forming and solving equations from word problems. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Keep the balance",
 "key_sub": "Do the same to both sides.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>An equation is like a balance: whatever you do to one side, do to the other.</li><li>Undo the operations in reverse order: 3x − 5 = 16 → 3x = 21 → x = 7.</li><li>For a word problem, let the unknown be x, write an equation and solve it. Check the answer in the story.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>5x + 4 = 29</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>5x = 25</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 5</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>2(x − 3) = 14</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>x − 3 = 7</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 10</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Doing different things to the two sides</td><td>Keep the balance.</td></tr><tr><td>Undoing in the wrong order</td><td>Undo + and − before × and ÷.</td></tr><tr><td>Not checking</td><td>Put the answer back in the equation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
